interpretation: |
  The 20 codebook bytes between the end of the staged
  docs/video/svq1/tables/codebook-l0l3.csv extraction window
  (file 0x62c00) and the true codebook upper boundary (file 0x62c14,
  where the embedded "BM" bitmap header begins).

  docs/video/svq1/audit/00-report.md pinned the codebook's functional
  base at file 0x5d214 (the single reloc-resolved static pointer from
  the SVC dispatch .text range, §2.3) and observed that the signed-VQ
  byte character extends past 0x62c00 to 0x62c14 (§2.5). The span
  0x5d214..0x62c14 is EXACTLY the canonical L=0..L=3 intra+inter sum
  of 23 040 bytes (spec/14 §14.4) — closing audit/00 §7 item 1's
  "16-byte gap" open item: the canonical codebook is
  [16 block-shape-LUT bytes at 0x5d214..0x5d224 (dual-use as the
  first vector bytes)] + [23 004 payload bytes at 0x5d224..0x62c00,
  staged as codebook-l0l3.csv] + [these 20 tail bytes].

  These 20 bytes are the tail of the LAST page — the L=0 level block's
  SECOND (inter) half: stage 6, vector 13 (bytes 4..8), vector 14, and
  vector 15 — pinned by locating the wiki §"Decoding Intraframe Plane
  Data" worked-example vectors (stage 1 vec 4 / stage 2 vec 14) at
  payload offsets 22288 / 22496, which places that page at canonical
  offset 22272..23040 ending exactly at 0x62c14. (The full page layout
  — level-major descending L=3..L=0, intra half then inter half per
  level — is pinned by the black-box intra conformance fixture in
  crates/oxideav-svq/tests/svq1_intra_conformance.rs.)
tool: python3 file read at the audit-pinned offsets; SHA-256 verified
  against the source_sha256 above before extraction
notes: |
  Byte-level data extraction only (a numeric table, no code or control
  flow). Staged locally because docs/video/svq1/tables/ does not yet
  carry this 20-byte window; the docs staging should backfill it (and
  the CSV here matches the codebook-l0l3.csv column format so it can
  be lifted verbatim).
